# Specification - Phase 2: UI Improvements & UX Polish

## Requirements

Implement core Taskwarrior WebUI UX improvements:

1. **#51 Pre-fill Project and Assignee on New Task**:
   - When the user is viewing a filtered project in the UI and clicks to add a new task, the "Project" field in the task creation dialog must be pre-filled with the active project.
   - When an assignee filter is active or available, pre-fill the "Assignee" field in the new task modal accordingly.

2. **#77 Bulk Add (Brain Dump Mode)**:
   - Streamline rapid successive task entry inside the "Add Task" modal.
   - Support keyboard shortcut `Ctrl+Enter` (or `Cmd+Enter` on macOS) to save the current task immediately and keep the modal open with description cleared and focus retained for the next entry.
   - Standard `Enter` or clicking "Save" adds the task and closes the modal as usual.

3. **#47 Date & Time Pickers for Task Dates**:
   - Integrate Vuetify date and time picker components (`v-date-picker` / `v-time-picker`) into task creation and edit dialogs for `due`, `wait`, and `scheduled` fields.
   - Maintain compatibility with textual relative expressions or quick buttons (e.g. today, tomorrow, eow).

4. **#74 & #22 Remember Sorting Order & Frontend Preferences**:
   - Persist user frontend preferences across page reloads using `localStorage`.
   - Store table sorting options (sort column, sort direction, items per page).
   - Ensure defaults are smoothly restored without layout jumping or state desync.

## User Stories
- As a user entering tasks under a specific project and assignee, I want those fields automatically pre-filled so I don't have to retype them repeatedly.
- As a user doing a brain dump of multiple tasks, I want to press `Ctrl+Enter` to rapidly submit task after task without having to reopen the dialog each time.
- As a user scheduling deadlines, I want visual date/time pickers to select dates accurately without manual text formatting.
- As a user who customized column sorting and page sizes, I want those preferences remembered when I refresh or revisit the page.
